{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["And the meaning of <b>one Torah</b>: apart from the burnt offerings, for the burnt offerings are under the obligation of a statute. And further HaShem said: \"When you bring a meal offering upon the burnt offering, of fine flour — so shall you give also from your oven-baked cakes.\" And there is no need to mention what our ancients of blessed memory received, for they are two — challah and terumah — and their measure is according to [each], for all their words are true and anything else is folly. Behold, an additional measure [applies] both where one unwittingly did what he was commanded not to do, and where one unwittingly failed to do what he was commanded to do."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:17:47.875668872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}